    Fix home-stop coordinates for return-home loop trips
    
    Bug: When the AI emitted the final return-home stop as type=DESTINATION
    (per the load-bearing first=HOME / last=DESTINATION invariant), the
    homeCoords backfill in createStop never fired because it only
    triggered on type === 'HOME'. Result: the final Mesa stop got
    latitude=null/longitude=null, and the trip map plotted the F (Finish)
    marker at generic Mesa city centroid instead of the user's actual
    home address (3145 N 76th Way, northeast Mesa).
    
    Audit-flagged on May 4: "StopType.HOME exists in the schema but the
    startup-migration block never writes it; possible drift between AI
    prompt emissions and DB state."
    
    Fix (server/src/controllers/trips.ts):
    - Extract normalizeCity from getTripMapImage's nested scope to module
      scope so it can be shared
    - createStop now also fetches homeCity and homeState from the user
    - Broaden homeCoords backfill condition: triggers on
      (type === 'HOME' || looksLikeHome) where looksLikeHome is true when
      normalizeCity(locationName) === user.homeCity (case-insensitive trim)
    - New distinct log line for the city-match path:
      [createStop:homeCoords] backfill via city match - locationName="..."
      matches homeCity="..." -> using home coords (...)
    
    Why not change the AI prompt instead:
    - The first=HOME / last=DESTINATION invariant is load-bearing.
      generateActivities and other downstream code filters on
      s.type === 'DESTINATION' && s.nights > 0. Letting the AI emit
      type: "HOME" for the return stop would silently change activity
      generation behavior. Coordinate backfill is the safer surface to
      patch.
    
    Why not extend the startup migration:
    - Same reason -- type is queried in many places, flipping
      return-home DESTINATIONs to HOME would have ripple effects.
    
    Edge case (theoretical, not blocking): if a user genuinely visits
    their home city for non-home reasons (e.g. lives in Phoenix and plans
    a stop "in Phoenix" meaning a campground in Phoenix), the backfill
    would override their desired location with home coords. In practice
    the AI doesn't emit stops at home city for non-home reasons, and any
    explicit lat/lng provided in the request body still wins (only fires
    when latitude is null/undefined).
    
    Verified end-to-end: planned a fresh "Phoenix to Flagstaff Loop"
    trip; new [createStop:homeCoords] backfill via city match log line
    fired for the final Mesa stop; trip map's F marker now lands at the
    user's actual home address (Las Sendas / NE Mesa) instead of city
    centroid.
    
    Known cosmetic inconsistency for next iteration:
    - Stops list shows asymmetric labels: first Mesa stop labeled "Start"
      but final Mesa stop labeled "Home / Finish". Both are the same
      physical location (user's home). Should be symmetric -- either both
      show "Home" framing or neither does. Filed for next session.
    
    Existing trip data: trips planned before this fix that have
    type=DESTINATION + null coordinates on a return-home final stop
    remain affected. Lowest-friction cleanup: delete-and-replan affected
    trips manually; only one currently identified (Phoenix Red Rock Loop,
    already deleted during testing).
